-#
  Cross-origin isolation is a property of the document and is only granted on a
  real navigation, so a Turbo visit would swap the body of a non-isolated
  document and silently lose it - taking SharedArrayBuffer, and the kernel, with
  it. This tells Turbo to do a full page load. Same as tracks/exercises/edit.
- content_for :meta_tags do
  %meta{ name: "turbo-visit-control", content: "reload" }

- require_stylesheet "editor"
- require_stylesheet "track"

= ReactComponents::Editor.new(@solution, experimental: true)
